/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E ( What I was unaware of was how much I enjoy learning about the field of neuroscience. I find the brain fascinating because there is so much that is unknown, and being able to dive deeper into my minor has allowed me to broaden my scope of learning and lean more into my curious side since I love learning new things. Discovering my new interest of neuroscience has allowed me to plan ahead for what I picture my future career to look like. My main goals are to be in the field of animal behaviour and/or specialize in neurology after completing a DVM. I feel that what I have learned in my program and minor has definitely prepared me for these potential career paths.  )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E ( To touch on some of my most memorable animal-based experiences, I have been an active volunteer at a vet clinic in my area since high school, where I have assisted with general practice duties such as restraining, prepping for surgery, maintenance around the clinic, walking animals, and, of course, learning from the head veterinarian. This experience has validated my passion for owning a clinic and provided valuable hands-on experience relevant to my education. I wanted to see if I was interested in research during my second year, so I helped a PhD student collect samples on a cow pasture for her project. This experience clarified that a research career was not for me, but I still gained valuable knowledge, which I will forever appreciate. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
