174 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 126 0 R
/E (When I did discover my passion for neuroscience, I volunteered at a wonderful specialty neurology hospital, where I got to dive deeper and see numerous spinal cord surgeries, MRIS, and shadow a veterinary neurologist taking appointments and diagnosing illnesses. This experience was extremely beneficial because I was able to immerse myself in the field of interest I am most interested in and learn what it is truly like to be in a busy referral Hospital. I was also a part of the Dairy Show for College Royal this year, which was so fun since I have not really had much large animal experience yet! For future plans, this summer, I am aiming to do a two-week study abroad program in Greece and I am so excited to travel to a new place and learn more about veterinary medicine. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
175 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 126 0 R
/E (Outside of school and animal-related experience, I am an active SafeWalk volunteer and future assistant coordinator. SafeWalk is an on-campus, safety, volunteer-based program that assists with walking students home after dark who would want accompaniment to their destination on campus, which has been a wonderful community to be a part of. Along with this, I am a fundraising executive for the Guelph Neuroscience Student Association, and I was a summer camp counsellor for Autism Ontario. During my free time, I enjoy watching shows and movies, with my favourites being The Big Bang Theory and any Harry Potter or Star Wars movies. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
